// prefer.storyarc
// part of Arcturus, a programming language and compiler for the Infocom Z-machine.
// Copyright (c) 2026, Stefan Vogt.
// https://github.com/ByteProject/Arcturus
//
// A showcase for the prefer seam (docs/01 chapter 14): the game's own say
// when a noun phrase ties between several things. Three coins in your purse
// all answer to "coin", so EXAMINE COIN is a genuine question and the
// parser asks it. But the ferry fare is a florin, and PAY COIN TO FERRYMAN
// should not ask what the story already knows: the game overrides `prefer`
// with a block that answers true for the florin while the action is give
// (the library's pay is a word of give). The matcher asks the block once
// per tied candidate, after a typed trigger and before the held tiebreak;
// exactly one preferred candidate wins silently, and in every other case
// the question happens as always. A game that never overrides the seam
// carries none of this. Compile and run:
//
//   arcc examples/features/prefer.storyarc -o prefer.z5
//   frotz prefer.z5
//
// Try, in order:
//   examine coin            three tie, nothing is preferred for examine: it asks
//   florin                  and the answer narrows, as always
//   pay coin to ferryman    the same three tie, and the florin is paid silently
//   pay coin to ferryman    two tie and neither is preferred: the honest question
//   sovereign               and the ferryman wants his florin

game
    title  "The Ferry"
    headline "A prefer showcase"
    author "Stefan Vogt"
    start  jetty

room jetty
    name "Jetty"
    desc "A weathered jetty over grey water. The ferry waits, and the
          ferryman holds out a hand. Your purse holds three coins."

thing ferryman of character in jetty
    name "ferryman"
    words ferryman, man

thing sovereign in player
    name "gold sovereign"
    words sovereign, gold, coin

thing florin in player
    name "silver florin"
    words florin, silver, coin

thing farthing in player
    name "copper farthing"
    words farthing, copper, coin

// The game's say in a tie: while paying (giving), the florin is the coin
// meant. Any other action leaves the tie to the parser's own rules.
block prefer(obj)
    if action is give
        if obj is florin
            return true
    return false

on give
    if second is ferryman
        if noun is florin
            move florin to ferryman
            say "The ferryman pockets the florin and waves you aboard."
        else
            say "The ferryman shakes his head. The fare is a florin."
    else
        continue
